rhizome-graph (26.08.001) unstable; urgency=medium

  * First numbered release, under the scheme CLAUDE.md now mandates: YY.MM.NNN,
    where NNN counts releases within the month and restarts at 001 when the
    month turns.
  * The version is NATIVE -- no Debian revision. A revision would be spelled
    `26.08.001-1`, and under the same scheme `-BB` already means the sequential
    bugfix of that exact release, so a packaging revision would read as a
    bugfix release that was never cut. Native versions cost nothing here: this
    package is built by packaging/build-deb.sh from this tree alone, and there
    is no separate upstream tarball for a revision to distinguish it from.
  * Note pyproject.toml declares the same number, but PEP 440 normalizes the
    padding away: `pip` and `rhi --version` report 26.8.1 for the release this
    changelog calls 26.08.001. The .deb, the tag and this file are exact.

 -- rhizome-graph contributors <brn.qi.home@gmail.com>  Tue, 25 Aug 2026 23:30:00 -0300

rhizome-graph (0.0.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial packaging. The version is the one pyproject.toml declares, plus a
    Debian revision; packaging/build-deb.sh reads it from the line above, so
    this file is the single place a release bumps.
  * Carries a virtualenv holding websockets alone, because the daemon imports
    websockets.asyncio.server and the version Debian ships predates it.
  * Carries the built front end at /usr/lib/rhizome-graph/web, which is where
    rhizome_graph/assets.py looks for it on an installed system. It is
    gitignored build output, so it must be built before the package is.

 -- rhizome-graph contributors <brn.qi.home@gmail.com>  Sun, 16 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0000
